    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "38e5a7b8cf1b92125cf8ce0dd579ccb4",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"two-loop-phi4-ibp-reduction-and-uv-poles\">Two-loop <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\phi^4||)</marimo-tex>: IBP reduction and UV poles</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse all notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/integral_families.py\">Integral families</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Reproduce the <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/Phi4/TwoLoops/Renormalization-SS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc two-loop self-energy example</a>\nusing <code>IntegralFamily</code>, the shared tensor reducer and the native IBP bridge.\nBoth Laporta elimination and a parametric recurrence run in this notebook.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The input is the reference's two scalar diagram integrands, with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(ig^2||)</marimo-tex>\nsuppressed: <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/(4D_1^2D_2)||)</marimo-tex> and\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/[6D_1D_2((k_1+k_2+p)^2-M)]||)</marimo-tex>, where <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(M=m^2&gt;0||)</marimo-tex>.\nDefine <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_1=k_1^2-M||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_2=k_2^2-M||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_3=(k_1+k_2)^2-M||)</marimo-tex>;\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I(a,b,c)||)</marimo-tex> integrates <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_1^{-a}D_2^{-b}D_3^{-c}||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p_2=p^2||)</marimo-tex>.\nTaylor expansion through <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2||)</marimo-tex> preserves their UV poles without introducing\nan infrared singularity. The tensor reducer supplies\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\langle(q\\cdot p)^2\\rangle=q^2p^2/d||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Analytic integral values enter later as reference inputs. The IBP search\ncomputes reduction coefficients; its residuals are <strong>not certified masters</strong>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
