          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"counterterm-recurrence-and-pole-cancellation\">Counterterm recurrence and pole cancellation</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The one-loop counterterm uses <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T(2)||)</marimo-tex>. Parametric IBP derives\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T(a+1)=(d-2a)T(a)/(2aM)||)</marimo-tex>, with its applicability conditions retained.\nInsert the one-loop constants <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(z_g^{(1)}=3/(2\\epsilon)||)</marimo-tex> and\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(z_m^{(1)}=1/(2\\epsilon)||)</marimo-tex> in units of <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(g/(16\\pi^2)||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">With <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(a=g/(16\\pi^2)||)</marimo-tex> the final reference result is\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_\\phi=1-\\frac{a^2}{24\\epsilon},\\qquad\n  Z_m=1+\\frac{a}{2\\epsilon}+a^2\\left[\\frac1{2\\epsilon^2}-\\frac5{24\\epsilon}\\right].||)</marimo-tex>$\nHere <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_m||)</marimo-tex> renormalizes the mass squared. The assertions check both constants\nand cancellation of all momentum, mass and logarithmic poles.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
